From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:36:22 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 61/87] Plutonium: zwp_text_input_v3 in Exo, for GTK 4, Qt 6
 and foot

Exo had only text-input-v1, which GTK 4, Qt 6 and foot don't speak, so
they got no input method. zwp_text_input_manager_v3 (version 1) runs on
the same TextInput as v1, with its own delegate:

- enter and leave follow the seat's keyboard focus, for the client's
  surfaces, not the input method's attachment.
- enable, disable, surrounding text, content type and cursor rectangle
  are double-buffered and applied on commit; enabling activates the
  TextInput on the entered surface, disabling or leaving deactivates it.
- the IME's composition, commits and deletions are preedit_string,
  commit_string and delete_surrounding_text (bytes around the selection),
  each followed by done with the number of commits as its serial.
- a key the IME consumed and passed on as a character is committed text,
  since v3 has no key events.

exo_unittests: TextInputV3Test drives the client's text input through
the TextInputClient, as an IME does.
